-- הודעת תכ"ם HOD.13.4.2.1 "לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית", מהדורה 15
-- (17.11.2022). The notice rewritten for the reform "דרך שווה" of 1.8.2022:
-- the tariffs by the distance between home and work, the allowance at the
-- monthly free pass "אוטובוס + רכבת", the equalisation supplement of
-- existing employees and its table, a move of address, trips on duty, the
-- income tax, and reporting in Malam. Its tables are DATA here, written by
-- tools/tariff_l4.py from the corpus and held to it by tests/test_tariffs.py.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `kitzuvat-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-common`

-- not weighed against `the Wage Protection Law`: the notice sets the
-- tariffs by which a travel EXPENSE is refunded (‘החזר בגין הוצאות’) and
-- the supplement that softens its cut; the income tax of 4.1-4.2 is
-- withheld by law, not a deduction the employer makes from wages.

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: ‘ימים בשבוע’ (4.1,
-- 4.2) is the basis of the tax withheld from the allowance, not the hours
-- of work and rest.

§ `הודעת תכ"ם 13.4.2.1 לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית — מהדורה 15`

`notice 15 is published` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 11 2022

§§ `1 רקע ומטרה`

-- 1.1 and 1.3: from 1.8.2022 the tariffs differ by the distance between
-- origin and destination and by the means (bus, or bus and train), as the
-- summary table of 1.3 prints them.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3
`the reform "Derech Shava" applies from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2022

-- tariff data akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3/t1 (tools/tariff_l4.py)
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3/t1
`notice 15's fare table 1` MEANS
    `a fare table` ""
        (LIST `a fare column` (JUST `a daily free pass`) (JUST `bus and train`) NOTHING, `a fare column` (JUST `a monthly free pass`) (JUST `bus and train`) NOTHING)
        (LIST `ranged` 0 (JUST 15) (LIST (JUST 18), (JUST 255)),
              `ranged` 15 (JUST 40) (LIST (JUST 28), (JUST 255)),
              `ranged` 40 (JUST 75) (LIST (JUST 37), (JUST 410)),
              `ranged` 75 (JUST 120) (LIST (JUST 42), (JUST 610)),
              `ranged` 120 (JUST 225) (LIST (JUST 74), (JUST 610)),
              `ranged` 255 NOTHING (LIST NOTHING, (JUST 610)))

-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 A pointer to the Ministry of Transport's page on the reform; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-4 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-5 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-5/p2 The agreement to soften the cut for existing employees (its rules are 2.2) and the notice's purpose; no rule.

§§ `2.1 כללי`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1 The heading "כללי"; its clauses follow.

-- 2.1.1 and 2.1.3: the refund is the relevant tariff, by the code reported
-- for the localities of home and work as the Derech Shava calculator gives
-- it: the monthly free pass "אוטובוס + רכבת" of the distance band (1.3).
-- The calculator is outside the corpus: the distance is the input.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
`the card notice 15 pays by` MEANS `bus and train`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
GIVEN km IS A NUMBER @desc the distance between home and work the calculator gives
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `notice 15's monthly allowance for the distance` km IS
    `the fare for the distance` `notice 15's fares` km `a monthly free pass` `the card notice 15 pays by`

-- 2.1.2: the salary accountant enters the calculator, gets the route's
-- tariffs, and reports the symbol with the tariff code (5.2).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tariff-notice duty`
DECIDE `finding and reporting the code, notice 15` IS
    PARTY `the salary accountant`
    MUST  `find the route's tariff code or distance on the Ministry of Transport's calculator`
    HENCE (PARTY `the salary accountant`
           MUST  `report the route's tariff code in the payroll`)

§§ `2.2 עובדים קיימים`

-- 2.2 and annex A: an existing employee was employed in a ministry or an
-- auxiliary unit on 31.7.2022; so is one employed that day whose employment
-- was broken afterwards for up to 6 months and resumed, or who moved to
-- another ministry or auxiliary unit, or home. A new employee is one taken
-- in from 1.8.2022, save those.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2 akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_2
GIVEN `employed on 31.7.2022` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months the employment was broken since` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 where it never was
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing employee under notice 15` `employed on 31.7.2022` `months the employment was broken since` IF
    `employed on 31.7.2022` AND `months the employment was broken since` AT MOST 6

-- 2.2.1-2.2.3: on top of the allowance, an existing employee is paid an
-- equalisation supplement. Where the allowance before the reform was below
-- the new tariff, the new tariff is paid (2.2.1); where the reform cut it by
-- less than 60 shekels against the highest of 2022 on the same route, the
-- new tariff, and no supplement (2.2.2); where by more than 60, the
-- supplement by the table: the allowance before the reform, X (every
-- component, the supplements of the 2018 reform included), less the row's
-- monthly reduction, and no lower than the row's floor (2.2.3). A cut of
-- exactly 60 is named by neither 2.2.2 nor 2.2.3; the table pays it no
-- supplement either way (X - 60 is the new tariff).
-- 2.2.3 also says the supplement is paid "בהתאם לתעריף "חופשי יומי –
-- אוטובוס + רכבת", אך לא יותר מתעריף זה", which names no amount the table
-- does not; the table governs (convention precedence.table; finding
-- F-…v15-b), as edition 16 rewrote the clause.
-- This edition sets one reduction, the table's monthly step "for a year";
-- the further reductions are edition 16's (2.2.4).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2/p2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3/p2
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER @desc the allowance paid before the reform, every component included
      `the new tariff` IS A NUMBER
      `the highest allowance of 2022` IS A NUMBER @desc on the same route
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `notice 15's equalisation supplement` x `the new tariff` `the highest allowance of 2022` IS
    IF `the highest allowance of 2022` MINUS `the new tariff` AT MOST `the cut that earns no supplement`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE `the equalisation supplement by the table` `notice 15's equalisation table` x `the new tariff` 1

`the cut that earns no supplement` MEANS 60

-- tariff data akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3/t1 (tools/tariff_l4.py)
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3/t1
`notice 15's equalisation table` MEANS
    LIST `an equalisation row` 1450 NOTHING (JUST 350) (JUST 1100) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 1300 (JUST 1450) (JUST 340) (JUST 980) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 1150 (JUST 1300) (JUST 320) (JUST 850) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 1000 (JUST 1150) (JUST 300) (JUST 730) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 850 (JUST 1000) (JUST 270) (JUST 610) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 750 (JUST 850) (JUST 240) (JUST 550) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 650 (JUST 750) (JUST 200) (JUST 490) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 550 (JUST 650) (JUST 160) (JUST 430) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 0 (JUST 550) (JUST 120) NOTHING (JUST 60)

-- Read as a cap, the daily free pass would hold the supplement the table
-- gives far below it: X of 1,500 on a route of 200 km, 830 by the table
-- against a daily pass of 74.
`notice 15's table pays more than the daily pass 2.2.3 names` MEANS
    fromMaybe 0 (`notice 15's equalisation supplement` 1500 610 1500)
        GREATER THAN fromMaybe 0 (`the fare for the distance` `notice 15's fares` 200 `a daily free pass` `bus and train`)
#ASSERT `notice 15's table pays more than the daily pass 2.2.3 names`

§§ `2.3 שינוי כתובת מגורים לעובדים קיימים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.3.1: the employee must tell human resources of a new address or
-- workplace; a move farther away keeps the supplement of 1.8.2022 without
-- recalculation (2.3.1.1); a move nearer leaves the new tariffs alone, no
-- supplement (2.3.1.2).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `reporting a move, notice 15` IS
    PARTY `the government employee`
    MUST  `report the new address or workplace on the travel-allowance form`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1__pnt_2-3-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1__pnt_2-3-1-2
GIVEN `the supplement of 1.8.2022` IS A NUMBER
      `the move is nearer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc by the reform's distance bands
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `notice 15's supplement after a move` `the supplement of 1.8.2022` `the move is nearer` IS
    IF `the move is nearer` THEN 0 ELSE `the supplement of 1.8.2022`

§§ `3 נסיעות בתפקיד`

-- 3.1-3.2: trips on duty are refunded at the daily free pass of the means
-- used ("חופשי יומי – אוטובוס" or "– אוטובוס + רכבת"): up to 1,000 shekels
-- a month to an employee with a service car, up to 1,500 to one with no car
-- standard, out of town, on report. 3.3: reported under symbol 1247.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-1 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-2
GIVEN `the daily passes of the trips on duty` IS A NUMBER
      `has a service car` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `notice 15's refund for trips on duty` `the daily passes of the trips on duty` `has a service car` IS
    min `the daily passes of the trips on duty` (IF `has a service car` THEN 1000 ELSE 1500)

@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tariff-notice duty`
DECIDE `reporting trips on duty, notice 15` IS
    PARTY `the salary accountant`
    MUST  `report the single trips on duty`

§§ `4 ניכוי מס הכנסה`

-- 4.1-4.2: income tax is withheld from the allowance up to 620 shekels a
-- month for an employee of a 6-day week, 527 for a 5-day week. No other
-- week is named (finding F-…v15-c; the instruction's own clause has the
-- same gap).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2
GIVEN allowance IS A NUMBER, `days a week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance notice 15 withholds tax from` allowance `days a week` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `days a week` EQUALS 6 THEN JUST (min allowance 620)
        IF `days a week` EQUALS 5 THEN JUST (min allowance 527)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

`notice 15 names no tax amount for a week of other than 5 or 6 days` MEANS
    isNothing (`the allowance notice 15 withholds tax from` 700 4)
#ASSERT `notice 15 names no tax amount for a week of other than 5 or 6 days`

§§ `5 אופן הדיווח`

-- akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-1 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-2 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-3 The headings of the two stages; their clauses follow.

-- 5.1-5.3: the distance band is taken from the Ministry's calculator (the
-- calculator shows the distance only), the monthly free pass of the band
-- read from the table of 1.3, and the tariff code reported in event 225.
-- 5.3.2 says the codes "start at 1000"; the table of 5.4 prints them 11.10
-- to 11.60, and the code reported is the table's.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-1__cls_5-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-1__cls_5-1-2 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-2__cls_5-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-2__cls_5-2-1__pnt_5-2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-2__cls_5-2-1__pnt_5-2-1-2 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-2__cls_5-2-1__pnt_5-2-1-3 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-2__cls_5-2-1__pnt_5-2-1-4 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-3__cls_5-3-1 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-3__cls_5-3-2 akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tariff-notice duty`
DECIDE `reporting the code in Malam, notice 15` IS
    PARTY `the salary accountant`
    MUST  `find the route's tariff code or distance on the Ministry of Transport's calculator`
    HENCE (PARTY `the salary accountant`
           MUST  `report the route's tariff code in the payroll`)

-- tariff data akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-4/t1 (tools/tariff_l4.py)
@ref akn:hc_1__para_5__subpara_5-4/t1
`notice 15's fare table 3` MEANS
    `a fare table` ""
        (LIST `a fare column` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING, `a fare column` (JUST `a monthly free pass`) NOTHING NOTHING)
        (LIST `banded` "11.10" "אזור צהוב" 0 (JUST 15) `bus and train` `a daily free pass` (LIST (JUST 18), (JUST 255)),
              `banded` "11.20" "אזור ירוק" 15 (JUST 40) `bus and train` `a daily free pass` (LIST (JUST 28), (JUST 255)),
              `banded` "11.30" "אזור תכלת" 40 (JUST 75) `bus and train` `a daily free pass` (LIST (JUST 37), (JUST 410)),
              `banded` "11.40" "אזור כחול" 75 (JUST 120) `bus and train` `a daily free pass` (LIST (JUST 42), (JUST 610)),
              `banded` "11.50" "אזור סגול" 120 (JUST 225) `bus and train` `a daily free pass` (LIST (JUST 74), (JUST 610)),
              `banded` "11.60" "אזור אפור" 225 NOTHING `bus and train` `a daily free pass` (LIST NOTHING, (JUST 610)))

-- akn:hc_1__para_6__subpara_6-1 akn:hc_1__para_6__subpara_6-2 The list of annexes; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p1 akn:att_2__hc_1/p2 akn:att_2__hc_1/t1 Annex B, the table of the editions' changes; a record, no rule.

§§ `המהדורה`

-- tariff data akn:all (tools/tariff_l4.py)
`notice 15's fare tables` MEANS
    LIST `notice 15's fare table 1`,
         `notice 15's fare table 3`

-- The summary table (1.3), which 2.1.3 and 5.2.1.4 pay by, is read first;
-- the table of codes (5.4) after it. The summary prints its last band
-- "מעל 255" where the bands before it close at 225 and the table of codes
-- opens its last at 225: between 225 and 255 km the summary prints no
-- tariff, and the table of codes is read (finding F-…v15-a).
`notice 15` MEANS
    `tariff notice` WITH
        `notice edition`       IS 15
        `notice published`     IS `notice 15 is published`
        `notice fares`         IS `notice 15's fares`
        `notice monthly means` IS JUST `the card notice 15 pays by`
        `notice unread codes`  IS concat (map `the misaligned codes of` `notice 15's fare tables`)

`notice 15's fares` MEANS concat (map `the fares of` `notice 15's fare tables`)

`notice 15's summary prints no tariff between 225 and 255 km` MEANS
    isNothing (`the fare for the distance` (`the fares of` `notice 15's fare table 1`) 240 `a monthly free pass` `bus and train`)
#ASSERT `notice 15's summary prints no tariff between 225 and 255 km`

§§ `Worked examples`

-- 30 km: the band of 15-40, 255 a month and 28 a day; on the shared bound
-- of 40 km, the band that opens there (thresholds.shared-bound): 410.
#ASSERT `notice 15's monthly allowance for the distance` 30 EQUALS JUST 255
#ASSERT `notice 15's monthly allowance for the distance` 40 EQUALS JUST 410
#ASSERT `notice 15's monthly allowance for the distance` 240 EQUALS JUST 610
#ASSERT `the fare for the distance` `notice 15's fares` 30 `a daily free pass` `bus and train` EQUALS JUST 28
-- Over 225 km no daily free pass is printed.
#ASSERT `the fare for the distance` `notice 15's fares` 300 `a daily free pass` `bus and train` EQUALS NOTHING

-- 2.2.3: X of 1,500 and a new tariff of 610: the row "1,450 and over"
-- leaves max(1,100, 1,500 - 60) = 1,440, a supplement of 830. A cut of 50
-- against 2022's highest earns none (2.2.2).
#ASSERT `notice 15's equalisation supplement` 1500 610 1500 EQUALS JUST 830
#ASSERT `notice 15's equalisation supplement` 660 610 660 EQUALS JUST 0
-- X of 500 (the row "0-550", no floor): 500 - 60 = 440 against a new
-- tariff of 255: 185.
#ASSERT `notice 15's equalisation supplement` 500 255 500 EQUALS JUST 185

#ASSERT `notice 15's supplement after a move` 300 TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `notice 15's refund for trips on duty` 1300 TRUE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `notice 15's refund for trips on duty` 1300 FALSE EQUALS 1300
#ASSERT `the allowance notice 15 withholds tax from` 700 5 EQUALS JUST 527
